Description: CVE-2026-125350, use-after-free in the cache of direct pattern matches (xsltTestCompMatch, libxslt/pattern.c); and CVE-2026-9947, a double free of the text of an xsl:attribute that is only whitespace under xml:space="preserve" (xsltAttribute, libxslt/attributes.c: its content, not of the dictionary, aliased as if it were); CVE-2025-10911, a use-after-free: the cached result tree fragments were kept in a list on the prev and next pointers of their xmlDoc, which an XPath evaluation could follow into freed documents; a list of its own now (the fields tmpRVT, persistRVT, localRVT, fragment and the RVT of the cache of xsltInternals.h become lists of type xsltRVTListPtr under new names, of the same size: neither libexslt nor ext/xsl of PHP use them; libxml2 2.15.2 and later already stop the traversal on their side, this is the fix of libxslt itself); CVE-2026-11196, a type confusion in xsltParseTemplateContent: a DTD in a template whose first child is a comment made it descend into the DTD and take an entity declaration for an element (a read past a heap buffer); CVE-2026-87636, document('') with a base URI that does not resolve gave the stylesheet itself to the transformation when it has no URL (one loaded from a string, as XSLTProcessor::importStylesheet() of a DOMDocument::loadXML() of PHP), where XSLT 1.0 (12.1) wants an empty node-set: a stylesheet that reads itself with document('') has to be loaded from a file (or given a URL, DOMDocument::$documentURI) now, from a string it gets an empty node-set and an I/O warning
Origin: Chromium third_party/libxslt/chromium/0008-Fix-use-after-free-in-direct-pattern-match-cache.patch (156.0.8078.96, Joey Arhar, 06.11.2026), as Gentoo carries it (dev-libs/libxslt files/libxslt-1.1.45-CVE-2026-125350.patch, bug 986081), -p0; CVE-2026-9947: Chromium (Andrew Paseltiner, 20.04.2026, bug 503627446), as Alpine carries it on 1.1.43 (main/libxslt CVE-2026-9947.patch, https://github.com/alpinelinux/aports/blob/master/main/libxslt/CVE-2026-9947.patch); libxslt master and Gentoo lack it; CVE-2025-10911: Daniel Cheng's fix of libxslt issue 144 (GNOME merge request 77, commit 953833a4, not in a release or master), as Red Hat carries it on 1.1.39 (RHEL 10, libxslt-1.1.39-CVE-2025-10911.patch) and Chromium https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/abf266b28588e4533242ca562ecb4be778d3e246 as Wolfi carries it on 1.1.45 (libxslt/CVE-2025-10911.patch): the same code on 1.1.45 (OpenBSD carried its earlier revision f94e7e97, with a doubly linked list, on 1.1.43); CVE-2026-11196: Chromium https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/f022d55a424e6b5727681af0002b9e185b3b808b (Andrew Paseltiner, 23.04.2026), as Wolfi carries it on 1.1.45; CVE-2026-87636: Chromium https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/8005fbd4ba5355dc88df069fd99bf76e3fd2b525 (31.07.2026), as Alpine carries it (main/libxslt CVE-2026-87636.patch, aports 945919c) and Wolfi; libxslt master after 1.1.45 has none of them (its d4ca6ed caches failed document() loads, 77d114f a crash of the profiling output: not taken)

